-- title:
--   Generic lift over W₀[[t]] is universal
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation ring $W_0$ which is a domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and which is adically complete for that ideal; let $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. (with the ideal $\bot$ taken as the ambient ideal) there is a unit power series $u$ over $k$ with $F_0.\mathtt{nthSeries}\,q = u \cdot F_0.\mathtt{drinfeldDivisor}\,q\,0\,0$, where $\mathtt{nthSeries}$ is the multiplication-by-$n$ series defined recursively by $[0] = 0$ and $[n+1] = F(\,[n],X\,)$. Let $F^u$ be a commutative formal group law over $W_0[\![t]\!]$ whose law is the image of that of $F_0$ under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, and assume the genericity condition that the coefficient of $t$ in the coefficient of $Z^q$ of $F^u.\mathtt{nthSeries}\,q$ is congruent to $1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$. The conclusion: for every commutative local Artinian $W_0$-algebra $T$ and every surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal of $T$ and with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \mathrm{algebraMap} = \mathrm{res}_0$, and every commutative formal group law $G$ over $T$ whose law is the image of that of $F_0$ under $\mathrm{res}_T$, there is exactly one $W_0$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : W_0[\![t]\!] \to T$ such that $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$ and such that there exist a formal group law $G'$ over $T$ whose law is the image of that of $F^u$ under $\varphi$ and an isomorphism $\psi : G' \to G$ of formal group laws (a power series with zero constant coefficient, unit linear coefficient, intertwining the two laws) whose series reduces to $X$ modulo the maximal ideal of $T$, in the sense that $\mathrm{res}_T$ of its $n$-th coefficient is $1$ for $n = 1$ and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the Lubin–Tate classification of deformations of a one-parameter formal group law of height two, in the form that a single explicitly given commutative lift $F^u$ over $W_0[\![t]\!]$ whose $q$-series has generic first-order coefficient already classifies all commutative lifts of $F_0$ to local Artinian $W_0$-algebras, rather than asserting the abstract existence of a universal deformation. It is used to identify complete local rings arising as deformation rings of formal groups — in particular towards regularity and Krull dimension two — and in the analysis of completions of moduli of elliptic curves with full level structure.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FormalGroup_IsDrinfeldBasisAdic_universal_deformation_powerSeries_of_generic_lift.lean

